sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: To cut a given finite straight line in extreme and mean ratio.
----
proof:

Let {AB} be the given finite straight line.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="280" height="350" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="VI.30 diagram" src="propVI30.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Describe the square BC on AB; apply to AC the parallelogram CD
    // (C, F, D and the unlettered corner N) with excess AD similar to BC
    // (VI.29). Then BF equals AD, so FE : ED = AE : EB (VI.14), and with
    // FE = AB, ED = AE the line is cut at E in extreme and mean ratio.
    //
    // Joyce's figure draws only the square ABHC, the square NAED and EF, so
    // AB is a solid slide twin over the square's side, hidden at rest
    // (initiallyHidden), for the slides before the square is described.
    // Everything else added is transparent: AC, AE, EB, ED, the parallelograms
    // CD, CE, BF (explicit ;0 faces), and the faceless twins BCt of ABHC and
    // ADt of NAED. ABHC's filled face would be raised over EF when
    // highlighted (#140), so the prose reaches the squares as {BC|BCt} and
    // {AD|ADt}. The equal angles at E of BF and AD are the right angles of
    // the squares, so they are marked as right angles.
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): only A and B, free — the
    // given line. H, C, N, E, D, F are derived and listed per slide.
    var GIVEN = ["A","B","AB"];
    var SQ    = GIVEN.concat(["ABHC","H","C"]);
    var APP   = SQ.concat(["NAED","N","E","D","F","EF"]);
    var ANG   = APP.concat(["rtBEF","rtAED"]);
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "VI.30",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;50,220",
            "B;point;free;220,220",
            "ABHC;polygon;square;A,B;0;0;black;random",
            "H;point;vertex;ABHC,3",
            "C;point;vertex;ABHC,4",
            "M;point;midpoint;A,C;0;0",
            "N;point;cutoff;M,A,M,B;0",
            "E;point;cutoff;A,B,A,N",
            "NAED;polygon;parallelogram;N,A,E;0;0;black;random",
            "D;point;vertex;NAED,4",
            "F;point;intersection;C,H,D,E",
            "EF;line;connect;E,F",
            // Slide twin, hidden at rest (see above).
            "AB;line;connect;A,B",
            // Transparent highlight targets; explicit ;0 faces.
            "AC;line;connect;A,C;0;0;0",
            "AE;line;connect;A,E;0;0;0",
            "EB;line;connect;E,B;0;0;0",
            "ED;line;connect;E,D;0;0;0",
            "BCt;polygon;quadrilateral;A,B,H,C;0;0;0;0",
            "ADt;polygon;quadrilateral;N,A,E,D;0;0;0;0",
            "CD;polygon;quadrilateral;C,F,D,N;0;0;0;0",
            "CE;polygon;quadrilateral;A,E,F,C;0;0;0;0",
            "BF;polygon;quadrilateral;E,B,H,F;0;0;0;0",
            "rtBEF;sector;angleMarkerRight;E,B,F,14;0;0;3b6ea5;9ec5e8",
            "rtAED;sector;angleMarkerRight;E,A,D,14;0;0;3b6ea5;9ec5e8"
        ],
        initiallyHidden: ["AB"],
        aliases: { "FE": "EF" },
        slides: [
            { text: "“To cut {a given finite straight line|AB} in extreme and mean ratio.”",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "VI.30" }] },
            { text: "Let {AB} be the given finite straight line.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB"] },
            { text: "It is required to cut {AB} in extreme and mean ratio.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB"] },
            { text: "Describe the square {BC|BCt} on {AB}.",
              visible: SQ,
              highlighted: ["BCt","AB"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "H",    name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "C",    name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "ABHC", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.46" }] },
            { text: "Apply the parallelogram {CD} to {AC} equal to the sum of {BC|BCt} and the figure {AD|ADt} similar to {BC|BCt}.",
              visible: APP,
              highlighted: ["CD","AC","ADt"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "N",    name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "E",    name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "D",    name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "NAED", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill },
                  { elem: "EF",   name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "F",    name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "CD applied to AC, exceeding by AD similar to BC", ref: "VI.29" }] },
            { text: "Now {BC|BCt} is a square, therefore {AD|ADt} is also a square.",
              visible: APP,
              highlighted: ["BCt","ADt"] },
            { text: "And, since {BC|BCt} equals {CD}, subtract {CE} from each,",
              visible: APP,
              highlighted: ["BCt","CD","CE"] },
            { text: "therefore the remainder {BF} equals the remainder {AD|ADt}.",
              visible: APP,
              highlighted: ["BF","ADt"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "BF = AD", ref: "C.N.3" }] },
            { text: "But it is also equiangular with it,",
              visible: ANG,
              highlighted: ["BF","ADt","rtBEF","rtAED"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "rtBEF", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "rtAED", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "therefore in {BF} and {AD|ADt} the sides about the equal angles are reciprocally proportional.",
              visible: ANG,
              highlighted: ["BF","ADt","rtBEF","rtAED"] },
            { text: "Therefore {FE} is to {ED} as {AE} is to {EB}.",
              visible: ANG,
              highlighted: ["EF","ED","AE","EB"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "FE : ED = AE : EB", ref: "VI.14" }] },
            { text: "But {FE} equals {AB}, and {ED} equals {AE}.",
              visible: ANG,
              highlighted: ["EF","AB","ED","AE"] },
            { text: "Therefore {AB} is to {AE} as {AE} is to {EB}.",
              visible: ANG,
              highlighted: ["AB","AE","EB"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AB : AE = AE : EB", ref: "V.7" }] },
            { text: "And {AB} is greater than {AE}, therefore {AE} is also greater than {EB}.",
              visible: ANG,
              highlighted: ["AB","AE","EB"] },
            { text: "Therefore the straight line {AB} has been cut in extreme and mean ratio at {E},",
              visible: ANG,
              highlighted: ["AB","E"] },
            { text: "and the greater segment of it is {AE}.",
              visible: ANG,
              highlighted: ["AE"],
              justifications: [
                  { claim: "AB cut in extreme and mean ratio", ref: "VI.Def.3" },
                  { ref: "Q.E.F." } ] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "VI.30") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "C.N.3":    "/elements/books/bookI/commonnotions/cn3/",
        "I.46":     "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI46/",
        "V.7":      "/elements/books/bookV/propositions/propV7/",
        "VI.14":    "/elements/books/bookVI/propositions/propVI14/",
        "VI.29":    "/elements/books/bookVI/propositions/propVI29/",
        "VI.Def.3": "/elements/books/bookVI/definitions/defVI3/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

It is required to cut {AB} in extreme and mean ratio.

Describe the square {BC|BCt} on {AB}.  Apply the parallelogram {CD} to {AC} equal to the sum of {BC|BCt} and the figure {AD|ADt} similar to {BC|BCt}. [!just I.46; VI.29]

Now {BC|BCt} is a square, therefore {AD|ADt} is also a square.

And, since {BC|BCt} equals {CD}, subtract {CE} from each, therefore the remainder {BF} equals the remainder {AD|ADt}.

But it is also equiangular with it, therefore in {BF} and {AD|ADt} the sides about the equal angles are reciprocally proportional. Therefore {FE} is to {ED} as {AE} is to {EB}. [!just VI.14]

But {FE} equals {AB}, and {ED} equals {AE}.

Therefore {AB} is to {AE} as {AE} is to {EB}. [!just V.7]

And {AB} is greater than {AE}, therefore {AE} is also greater than {EB}.

Therefore the straight line {AB} has been cut in extreme and mean ratio at {E}, and the greater segment of it is {AE}. [!just VI.Def.3]

<div class="qed">Q.E.F.</div>
<br clear="all">
----
guide:

The construction given here cuts a line into two parts *A* and *B* so that
(*A* + *B*):*B* = *B* : *A.*
By proposition @VI.17, that condition is equivalent to making the rectangle *A* + *B* by *A* equal the square *B* by *B,* and that is the construction of proposition @II.11.

#### Use of this proposition

This construction is used in @XIII.17 to construct a pentagonal face of a regular dodecahedron.
